{
  "book": "Amos",
  "commentary": "Darby Translation Notes",
  "author": "John Nelson Darby",
  "entries": [
    {
      "start_chapter": 1,
      "start_verse": 1,
      "end_chapter": 1,
      "end_verse": 1,
      "title": "",
      "content": "(h-0) * (The title of this Book, 'Amos'), Said to mean, 'Burden-bearer.' herdmen (i-9) Or 'sheepmasters,' 2Kings 3.4. Tekoa, (k-11) In Judah, 2Chron. 11.6."
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 1,
      "start_verse": 2,
      "end_chapter": 1,
      "end_verse": 2,
      "title": "",
      "content": "pastures (a-16) or 'habitations.' see Jer. 9.10; 23.10; 25.37, &c."
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 1,
      "start_verse": 5,
      "end_chapter": 1,
      "end_verse": 5,
      "title": "",
      "content": "bar (b-6) See Deut. 3.5. valley (c-16) Or 'plain.' see Note, Josh. 11.8. Aven, (d-18) Or 'valley of idols.' Beth-Eden; (e-26) Meaning, 'House of delight.'"
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 1,
      "start_verse": 6,
      "end_chapter": 1,
      "end_verse": 6,
      "title": "",
      "content": "sentence; (f-17) Lit. 'revoke it.' see ver. 3."
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 1,
      "start_verse": 8,
      "end_chapter": 1,
      "end_verse": 8,
      "title": "",
      "content": "Jehovah. (g-37) Adonai Jehovah. see Note b, Ezek. 2.4."
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 1,
      "start_verse": 11,
      "end_chapter": 1,
      "end_verse": 11,
      "title": "",
      "content": "pity; (h-30) Lit. 'destroyed his mercies.'"
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 2,
      "start_verse": 7,
      "end_chapter": 2,
      "end_verse": 7,
      "title": "",
      "content": "after (a-2) Or, 'they who pant after.'"
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 2,
      "start_verse": 8,
      "end_chapter": 2,
      "end_verse": 8,
      "title": "",
      "content": "condemned. (b-27) Or 'those that are amerced.'"
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 2,
      "start_verse": 11,
      "end_chapter": 2,
      "end_verse": 11,
      "title": "",
      "content": "saith (c-26) See Isa. 1.24."
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 2,
      "start_verse": 13,
      "end_chapter": 2,
      "end_verse": 13,
      "title": "",
      "content": "you, (d-6) Lit. 'in your place.' Others, 'I am pressed under you (i.e. 'your sins') as the cart is loaded with sheaves.'"
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 2,
      "start_verse": 14,
      "end_chapter": 2,
      "end_verse": 14,
      "title": "",
      "content": "flight (e-2) Or 'refuge,' as Jer. 25.35."
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 3,
      "start_verse": 6,
      "end_chapter": 3,
      "end_verse": 6,
      "title": "",
      "content": "[it]? (f-27) Or 'not have acted.'"
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 3,
      "start_verse": 9,
      "end_chapter": 3,
      "end_verse": 9,
      "title": "",
      "content": "in (g-2) in (g-8) Or 'upon.'"
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 3,
      "start_verse": 12,
      "end_chapter": 3,
      "end_verse": 12,
      "title": "",
      "content": "couch, (a-41) The best place of the divan in the houses of the rich."
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 3,
      "start_verse": 13,
      "end_chapter": 3,
      "end_verse": 13,
      "title": "",
      "content": "in (b-5) Or 'against.'"
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 4,
      "start_verse": 3,
      "end_chapter": 4,
      "end_verse": 3,
      "title": "",
      "content": "Harmon, (c-21) Some translate 'to the mountains,' others, 'to the [enemy's] fortress,' or 'to the palace,' as in ch. 1.4, &c.. the meaning is not ascertained."
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 4,
      "start_verse": 4,
      "end_chapter": 4,
      "end_verse": 4,
      "title": "",
      "content": "days, (d-21) Perhaps 'years;' 'days' in Hebrew is used for 'years,' but here probably it is in irony."
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 4,
      "start_verse": 5,
      "end_chapter": 4,
      "end_verse": 5,
      "title": "",
      "content": "burn (e-2) 'Burn as incense.' see Lev. 1.9."
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 4,
      "start_verse": 9,
      "end_chapter": 4,
      "end_verse": 9,
      "title": "",
      "content": "palmer-worm (f-10) See Joel 1.4."
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 5,
      "start_verse": 3,
      "end_chapter": 5,
      "end_verse": 3,
      "title": "",
      "content": "forth (a-11) i.e. that contributed a thousand men for war. cf. Judg. 11.3 and Note."
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 5,
      "start_verse": 5,
      "end_chapter": 5,
      "end_verse": 5,
      "title": "",
      "content": "nought. (b-26) The Hebrew for 'nought' is here Aven, 'vanity,' 'iniquity.' see Hos. 4.15."
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 5,
      "start_verse": 11,
      "end_chapter": 5,
      "end_verse": 11,
      "title": "",
      "content": "pleasant (c-33) Or 'excellent.'"
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 5,
      "start_verse": 12,
      "end_chapter": 5,
      "end_verse": 12,
      "title": "",
      "content": "bribe, (d-20) 1Sam. 12.3."
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 5,
      "start_verse": 22,
      "end_chapter": 5,
      "end_verse": 22,
      "title": "",
      "content": "offer (a-4) Lev. 14.20."
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 5,
      "start_verse": 26,
      "end_chapter": 5,
      "end_verse": 26,
      "title": "",
      "content": "Moloch, (b-9) i.e. Milcom. Others render it 'your King.' Chiun (c-11) Some understand Chiun as the 'stand of the idol.' The LXX reads, 'star of your god Remphan.' see Acts 7.43."
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 6,
      "start_verse": 1,
      "end_chapter": 6,
      "end_verse": 1,
      "title": "",
      "content": "secure (d-13) Or 'careless,' as Isa. 32.9. first (e-23) Or 'named the chief;' but cf. Num. 24.20."
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 6,
      "start_verse": 6,
      "end_chapter": 6,
      "end_verse": 6,
      "title": "",
      "content": "breach (f-19) Or 'destruction.' see Lam. 3.48."
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 6,
      "start_verse": 7,
      "end_chapter": 6,
      "end_verse": 7,
      "title": "",
      "content": "captive, (g-12) Lit. 'at the head of the captives'"
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 6,
      "start_verse": 8,
      "end_chapter": 6,
      "end_verse": 8,
      "title": "",
      "content": "himself, (h-7) Lit. 'his soul.'"
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 6,
      "start_verse": 10,
      "end_chapter": 6,
      "end_verse": 10,
      "title": "",
      "content": "uncle, (i-4) Or 'next relation.'"
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 6,
      "start_verse": 13,
      "end_chapter": 6,
      "end_verse": 13,
      "title": "",
      "content": "power (k-18) Lit. 'horns.'"
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 6,
      "start_verse": 14,
      "end_chapter": 6,
      "end_verse": 14,
      "title": "",
      "content": "Arabah. (a-37) Deut. 1.1 and 2Kings 14.25."
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 7,
      "start_verse": 1,
      "end_chapter": 7,
      "end_verse": 1,
      "title": "",
      "content": "locusts (b-13) Heb. gob. see Nah. 3.17."
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 7,
      "start_verse": 4,
      "end_chapter": 7,
      "end_verse": 4,
      "title": "",
      "content": "inheritance. (c-29) Lit. 'lot,' 'portion,' Num 18.20."
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 7,
      "start_verse": 14,
      "end_chapter": 7,
      "end_verse": 14,
      "title": "",
      "content": "gatherer (d-25) Or 'dresser.'"
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 7,
      "start_verse": 16,
      "end_chapter": 7,
      "end_verse": 16,
      "title": "",
      "content": "[words] (e-18) Lit. 'drop not.' see Job 29.22; Ezek. 20.46; 21.2; Mic. 2.6,11."
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 8,
      "start_verse": 3,
      "end_chapter": 8,
      "end_verse": 3,
      "title": "",
      "content": "palace (f-6) Or 'temple.' Silence! (a-31) See ch. 6.10."
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 8,
      "start_verse": 4,
      "end_chapter": 8,
      "end_verse": 4,
      "title": "",
      "content": "poor (b-15) Lit. 'meek,' or 'afflicted,' as Ps. 9.18."
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 8,
      "start_verse": 9,
      "end_chapter": 8,
      "end_verse": 9,
      "title": "",
      "content": "land (c-30) Or 'the earth.'"
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 8,
      "start_verse": 14,
      "end_chapter": 8,
      "end_verse": 14,
      "title": "",
      "content": "sin (d-6) Elsewhere also 'trespass.'"
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 9,
      "start_verse": 1,
      "end_chapter": 9,
      "end_verse": 1,
      "title": "",
      "content": "them (e-37) Or 'their posterity,' as ch. 4.2; Ps. 109.13."
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 9,
      "start_verse": 7,
      "end_chapter": 9,
      "end_verse": 7,
      "title": "",
      "content": "Ethiopians (f-8) Heb. 'Cushites.' Caphtor, (a-33) See Gen. 10.14."
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 9,
      "start_verse": 11,
      "end_chapter": 9,
      "end_verse": 11,
      "title": "",
      "content": "tabernacle (b-9) Or 'booth.' 'hut,' 2Sam. 11.11; Ps. 76.2."
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 9,
      "start_verse": 12,
      "end_chapter": 9,
      "end_verse": 12,
      "title": "",
      "content": "Edom, (c-8) The LXX and their followers would seem to have read 'men,' and hence the application in Acts 15.17. But the manuscripts with one voice have 'Edom.' There can be no doubt that it is right."
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 9,
      "start_verse": 14,
      "end_chapter": 9,
      "end_verse": 14,
      "title": "",
      "content": "turn (d-4) Ps. 14.7 and 126.1."
    }
  ]
}
